"hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2729,"###
 Ya'qub ad-Dawraqi narrated to us, stating that Hushaym narrated to us, who informed us that Ata' bin as-Sa'ib narrated from Abdullah bin Ubayd bin Umair, who said: ""I heard my father saying to Ibn Umar: 'Why is it that I do not see you touching (istilam) except these two corners, the Black Stone and the Yemeni Corner?' Ibn Umar replied: 'If I do so, it is because I heard the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ"
2730,"Yusuf bin Musa narrated to us, saying: Jarir narrated to us. And Ali bin Al-Mundhir narrated to us, saying: Ibn Fudail narrated to us. And Al-Hasan bin Az-Za'farani narrated to us, saying: Ubaidullah bin Ubaid bin Umair narrated to us, from his father, from Ibn Umar (RA), from the Prophet (ﷺ), with a narration similar to the previous one."
